---
import Cmd from "../components/Cmd.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PowerTimeline from "../components/PowerTimeline.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const path = "/power/";
---

<Base
  title="Power | Kiln"
  description="Every Kiln VM has a power mode. Idle machines stop after a timeout and wake on the next request."
  path={path}
>
  <PageHeader
    slot="header"
    path={path}
    title="Idle machines stop. Use wakes them."
    lead="Every VM has a power mode. Use means an exec, a terminal, an upload or download, a proxied HTTP request or an open forward."
  >
    <div slot="aside" class="stack-cmds">
      <Cmd line="kiln vm create app --profile ubuntu-docker --power on_demand --idle 10m" />
      <Cmd line="kiln vm power app --mode warm --idle 15m" />
    </div>
  </PageHeader>

  <Section id="s-modes" title="One timeline under each of the four modes.">
    <PowerTimeline />
  </Section>

  <Section id="s-wake" title="What a wake looks like.">
    <div class="quads quads--stems">
      <div>
        <h3 class="sub">The request that wakes a VM gets an answer</h3>
        <p>
          For a minute after a VM starts, the HTTP proxy retries refused connections until the guest service listens.
          After that minute a refused connection returns 502 at once.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="sub">An open forward keeps it awake</h3>
        <p>
          Each connection through <code>kiln vm forward</code> wakes the VM when its mode allows that. The VM does not
          idle-stop while the connection stays open.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="sub">Opening a terminal starts a stopped VM</h3>
        <p>
          <code>kiln vm open</code> starts the VM, waits for the guest agent and attaches. A VM in
          <code>manual</code> mode is the exception. Start it yourself first.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="sub">A daemon restart stops every VM</h3>
        <p>
          When <code>kilnd</code> shuts down, it stops the VMs that are running. On its next start, VMs in
          <code>always</code> and <code>warm</code> mode boot again on the same disk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="zones zones--gap">
      <div class="zones__k">
        <p class="lead">Read a VM's mode, or change it. The new mode applies to the VM you already have.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="zones__iln stack-cmds">
        <Cmd line="kiln vm power app" />
        <Cmd line="kiln vm power app --mode manual" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
